0,Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Trans–New Guinea is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.",Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
1,Binumarien Language (BJR) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bjr/,Binumarien is a stable indigenous language of Papua New Guinea . It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
2,Afaqina [Newguineaworld],https://newguineaworld.linguistik.uzh.ch/families/trans-new-guinea/eastern-highlands-kratke-range/eastern-highlands/kainantu/east-kainantu/afaqina,Trans New Guinea. Asmat-Muli Strait. Asmat-Kamrau Bay.The term Binumarien refers to a now-abandoned village which was called Pinumaarénai. The Afaqina population was decimated by exposure to malaria after being driven into the Markham valley by warfare.,Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
3,Binumarien | Accent Network,https://accentnetwork.com/binumarien/,"Binumarien language, Papua New Guinea. Trans-New Guinea language family. Spoken in Eastern Highlands Province.",Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
4,Binumarien language and alphabet,https://omniglot.com/writing/binumarien.htm,Binumarien is a member of the Kainantu-Goroka group of Trans-New Guinea language family.,Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
5,Binumarien - bjr (Trans-New Guinea) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/bjr/,"Binumarien (bjr) is part of the Trans-New Guinea family and Trans-New Guinea, Kainantu-Goroka, Kainantu, Tairora class.",Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
6,database of the languages of New Guinea,https://transnewguinea.org/language/binumarien,"Sources: Xiao (1990). Classification: Nuclear Trans New Guinea, Kainantu-Goroka, Kainantu, Tairora.",Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
7,Binumarien Language Sample | Language Museum,https://www.language-museum.com/encyclopedia/b/binumarien.php,"If you want to get a flavour of the Binumarien language, check out a small sample at the Language Museum.There was evening, then morning, the first day. Statistics. Papua New Guinea (360) - Total (360). Classification. Trans-New Guinea | Main Section.",Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
8,"van Dasselaar | Binumarien (Eastern Highlands, Papua New Guinea)...",https://www.lddjournal.org/article/id/1215/,"Binumarien is a Papuan language spoken by an ethnic group of the same name in the Kainantu District of the Eastern Highlands Province in Papua New Guinea. According to local estimates, the language has approximately 1,200 speakers.",Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
9,How the Binumarien people of New Guinea discovered Jesus is real,https://creation.com/en/articles/binumarien-people-find-bible-true,"To the Binumariens, the truth of the scriptures was now beyond doubt. References. Lynette Oates, Hidden People: How a remote New Guinea culture was brought back from the brink of extinction, Albatross Books, Sutherland, NSW, pp. 205–207, 1992.",Binumarien,Trans-New Guinea
